0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Three switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   0   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   1   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
0000                LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
0000                SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; gap after z: a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0100                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0100                          IF   1-EDGEN   
0100   31 FC 09               LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   EDGEN   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
                              LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
                              JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
                              NOP      ; 07  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   CPM   
0103   C3 6F 07               JP   start   ; 03
0106   00 00                  DW   0   ; 06  spare
0108                          ENDIF      
0108                VECS:        
0108                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0108   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0109   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
010A   23                     INC   HL   
010B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
010C   23                     INC   HL   
010D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
010E   D9                     EXX      
010F   D1                     POP   DE   
0110   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0111                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0111   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0113   20 1F                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0115   C3 95 04     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0118                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0118   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0119   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
011A   18 15                  JR   nx   
011C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
011D   CF                     RST   08h   
011E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
011F   F7                     RST   30h   
0120                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0120   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0121   95                     SUB   L   
0122   6F                     LD   L,A   
0123   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0124   94                     SUB   H   
0125   67                     LD   H,A   
0126   C9                     RET      
0127   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0128                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0128                RST28:       
0128                          IFN   CPM   
                    PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
0128                          ENDIF      
0128                          IF   CPM   
0128   C3 D2 03               JP   putc   ; 28
012B                          ENDIF      
012B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
012C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
012D   C3 B2 01               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0130                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0130   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0131                NX:          
0131                          IF   CPM   
0131   C3 34 01               JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0134                          ENDIF      
0134                VECEND:      
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0134                             ; 
0134                             ;    00h          end of program
0134                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0134                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0134                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0134                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0134                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                NEXT0:       
0134                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0134                          ENDIF      
0134   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0135   03                     INC   BC   
0136   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
0138   38 D7                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
013A   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
013C   38 22                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
013E   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0140   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
0142   38 58                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0144   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0146   38 16                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
0148   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
014A   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
014C   38 5A                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
014E   FE 20                  CP   20h   
0150   38 0A                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0152   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0154   38 4C                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0156   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
0158                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0158   30 DA                  JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
015A                          ENDIF      
015A                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
                              JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
015A                          ENDIF      
015A   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
015C   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
015E   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0160                .macro PTABLE,
0160                             ; 
0160                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
0160                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
0160                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
0160                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
0160                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0160                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
0160                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0160                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0160                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
0160                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
0160                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
0160                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
0160                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
0160                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
0160                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
0160                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
0160                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0160                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
0160                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
0160                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
0160                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
0160                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
0160                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
0160                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
0160                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
0160                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
0160                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
0160                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
0160                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
0160                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
0160                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
0160                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
0160                .endm
0160                 
0160                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0160                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0160   C6 60        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0162   5F                     LD   E,A   
0163   16 03                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
0165   FE 76                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0167   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
0168   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0169                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
                              LD   D,0   
0169                          ENDIF      
0169                          IFN   CPM   
                              RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
0169                          ENDIF      
0169                          IF   CPM   
0169   16 01                  LD   D,1   
016B   30 01                  JR   NC,pu1   
016D   14                     INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
016E                PU1:         
016E                          ENDIF      
016E   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
016F   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0170                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
0170                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
0170                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
0170                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
0170                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
0170                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
0170                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                    ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CPM)   
                              LD   H,A   ; (A = 0) no key is held, and the break key
                              LD   L,A   ;   is on (the checked build has cleared
0170                          ENDIF      ;   these)
0170                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*CPM   
                              LD   HL,0   
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                          IF   1-EDITOR   
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
0170                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
0170                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
0170                          IF   TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
0170                          ENDIF      
0170                             ; =============================================================================
0170                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0170                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
0170                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
0170                             ; =============================================================================
0170   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
0171   7C                     LD   A,H   
0172   AA                     XOR   D   
0173   67                     LD   H,A   
0174   7D                     LD   A,L   
0175   AB                     XOR   E   
0176   6F                     LD   L,A   
0177   F7                     RST   30h   
0178   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
0179   7C                     LD   A,H   
017A   B2                     OR   D   
017B   67                     LD   H,A   
017C   7D                     LD   A,L   
017D   B3                     OR   E   
017E   6F                     LD   L,A   
017F   F7                     RST   30h   
0180   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
0181   2B                     DEC   HL   
0182   F7                     RST   30h   
0183                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0183                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0183   ED 5B 7C 0A  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
0187                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
0187                          ENDIF      
0187   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
0188                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkhp   
0188                          ENDIF      
0188   22 7C 0A               LD   (HEAP),HL   
018B   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
018C   F7                     RST   30h   
018D   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
018E   22 34 0A               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
0191   D9                     EXX      
0192   CD 2B 01               CALL   jphl   
0195   D9                     EXX      
0196   2A 34 0A               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
0199   D9                     EXX      
019A   E1                     POP   HL   
019B   F7                     RST   30h   
019C                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
019C                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
019C                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
019C   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
019D   0B                     DEC   BC   
019E   CD 03 03               CALL   rdnum   
01A1   F7                     RST   30h   
01A2                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
01A2   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
01A3   87                     ADD   A,A   
01A4   6F                     LD   L,A   
01A5   26 0A                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
01A7   F7                     RST   30h   
01A8                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
01A8                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
01A8   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
01A9   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
01AA   87                     ADD   A,A   
01AB   6F                     LD   L,A   
01AC   26 0A                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
01AE   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
01AF   2C                     INC   L   
01B0   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
01B1   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
01B2                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
01B2                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
01B2                             ; 
01B2                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
01B2                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
01B2                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
01B2                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop four bytes and 14 T-states.
01B2                             ; (DEC B, not DJNZ: its zero flag lasts through the EXX, so one EXX serves
01B2                             ; both ways out.)
01B2   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
01B3   D1                     POP   DE   
01B4   2B                     DEC   HL   
01B5   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01B6   2B                     DEC   HL   
01B7   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01B8   05                     DEC   B   
01B9   D9                     EXX      
01BA   CC 92 03               CALL   Z,pollk   
01BD   F7                     RST   30h   
01BE                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
01BE                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
01BE                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
01BE                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
01BE                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
01BE                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
01BE                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01BE   CD 80 03     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
01C1   30 CA                  JR   NC,exec   
01C3   77           HX1:      LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
01C4   CD 80 03               CALL   hexc   
01C7   30 08                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
01C9   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
01CB   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
01CC   CD 80 03               CALL   hexc   
01CF   38 F2                  JR   C,hx1   
01D1   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
01D3   F7                     RST   30h   
01D4                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01D4                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01D4                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01D4                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01D4                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01D4                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
01D4   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
01D5   42                     LD   B,D   
01D6   4B                     LD   C,E   
01D7   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
01D8                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01D8                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01D8   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
01D9   B5                     OR   L   
01DA   E1                     POP   HL   
01DB   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
01DD   CD 25 03               CALL   skip   
01E0   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01E1   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
01E3   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
01E4   F7                     RST   30h   
01E5                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01E5                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01E5                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01E5                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01E5                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01E5   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
01E6   03                     INC   BC   
01E7   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
01E9   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
01EA   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
01EC   FE 1A                  CP   26   
01EE   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
01F0   CB 23                  SLA   E   
01F2   16 0A                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
01F4   79                     LD   A,C   
01F5   12                     LD   (DE),A   
01F6   1C                     INC   E   
01F7   78                     LD   A,B   
01F8   12                     LD   (DE),A   
01F9   18 03                  JR   skipnx   
01FB                DEF2:        
01FB                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   " "-"A"+256   
                              JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
01FB                          ENDIF      
01FB   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
01FC   60                     LD   H,B   
01FD   69                     LD   L,C   
01FE                SKIPNX:      
01FE                          IF   CHECKED   
                              DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
01FE                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
01FE   CD 25 03     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
0201   F7                     RST   30h   
0202   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
0203   23                     INC   HL   
0204   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0205   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0206   F7                     RST   30h   
0207                             ; =============================================================================
0207                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0207                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0207                             ;  page.
0207                             ; =============================================================================
0207                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0207                             ; the matching ")".
0207   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0208   B5                     OR   L   
0209   E1                     POP   HL   
020A   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
020C   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
020D   18 A3                  JR   rpushn   
020F                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
020F                             ; drops it and carries on.
020F   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
0210   B5                     OR   L   
0211   E1                     POP   HL   
0212   28 CF                  JR   Z,rdrop   
0214   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
0215   42                     LD   B,D   
0216   4B                     LD   C,E   
0217   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0218   18 98                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
021A                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
021A                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
021A   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
021B   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
021D   FE 0A                  CP   10   
021F   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
0221   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
0222   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
0223   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0224   F7                     RST   30h   
0225   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0226   CD 03 03               CALL   rdnum   
0229   E7                     RST   20h   
022A   F7                     RST   30h   
022B   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
022C   7C                     LD   A,H   
022D   A2                     AND   D   
022E   67                     LD   H,A   
022F   7D                     LD   A,L   
0230   A3                     AND   E   
0231   6F                     LD   L,A   
0232   F7                     RST   30h   
0233                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
0233                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
0233                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
0233                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
0233   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
0234   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
0235   7C                     LD   A,H   
0236   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0238   67                     LD   H,A   
0239   7A                     LD   A,D   
023A   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
023C   57                     LD   D,A   
023D   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
023F   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
0241   F7                     RST   30h   
0242   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
0243   B7                     OR   A   
0244   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0246   7C                     LD   A,H   
0247   B5                     OR   L   
0248   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
024A   18 F3                  JR   tf   
024C                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
024C                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
024C   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
024D   C5                     PUSH   BC   
024E   7C                     LD   A,H   
024F   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
0250   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0253   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0255   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0256   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0258   17                     RLA      
0259   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
025B   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
025C   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
025E   C1                     POP   BC   
025F   F7                     RST   30h   
0260                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
0260                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
0260                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
0260                             ; stops on it.
0260                H_DIV:       
0260                          IF   CHECKED   
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JP   Z,e_zero   
0260                          ENDIF      
0260   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
0261   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; free BC for udiv
0262   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
0263   7A                     LD   A,D   
0264   AC                     XOR   H   
0265   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
0266   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0268   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
026B   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
026C   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
026E   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
0271   CD DD 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
0274   F1                     POP   AF   
0275   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
0278   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
0279   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
027A   B7                     OR   A   
027B   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
027E   C1                     POP   BC   
027F   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
0280   F7                     RST   30h   
0281                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
0281   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
0282   F7                     RST   30h   
0283   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
0284   F7                     RST   30h   
0285                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
0285                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
0285                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
0285                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkst   
0285                          ENDIF      
0285   D1                     POP   DE   
0286   73                     LD   (HL),E   
0287   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
0288                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
0288                          IF   CHECKED   
                              CALL   chkst   
0288                          ENDIF      
0288   D1                     POP   DE   
0289   73                     LD   (HL),E   
028A   23                     INC   HL   
028B   72                     LD   (HL),D   
028C   DF                     RST   18h   
028D                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
028D                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
028D   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
028E   60                     LD   H,B   
028F   69                     LD   L,C   
0290   CD 1A 03               CALL   skipstr   
0293                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
                              JP   Z,e_quote   
0293                          ENDIF      
0293   F7                     RST   30h   
0294                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
0294                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
0294                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
0294                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   Z,pr9   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,pr1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              AND   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   h_print   
0294                          ENDIF      
0294                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
                                 ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
                                 ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
                    H_PRINT:   PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   prstr   
                              POP   DE   
                              RST   18h   
0294                          ENDIF      
0294                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
0294                             ; (With the editor the loop is a routine, prstr, which ^V uses too.)
0294   CD 3E 04     H_PRINT:   CALL   prstr   
0297   DF                     RST   18h   
0298                          ENDIF      
0298   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
0299   EF                     RST   28h   
029A   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
029B                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
029B   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   BC   
029C   CD 46 03               CALL   psgn   
029F   C1                     POP   BC   
02A0   DF                     RST   18h   
02A1                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02A1                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02A1                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02A1                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02A1                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02A1   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
02A3   20 19                  JR   NZ,line   
02A5   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
02A7   CD C0 03     KT2:      CALL   getk   
02AA   20 0E                  JR   NZ,kt3   
02AC   1D                     DEC   E   
02AD   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
02AF   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
02B0   B5                     OR   L   
02B1   28 F2                  JR   Z,kt1   
02B3   2B                     DEC   HL   
02B4   7C                     LD   A,H   
02B5   B5                     OR   L   
02B6   20 ED                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
02B8   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
02B9   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
02BA   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
02BB   26 00                  LD   H,0   
02BD   F7                     RST   30h   
02BE                          IF   CPM   
02BE                             ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
02BE                             ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
02BE   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
02C1   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
02C2   9F                     SBC   A,A   
02C3   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
02C4   EE 7F                  XOR   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
02C6   32 7E 0A               LD   (LBHDR),A   
02C9   11 7E 0A               LD   DE,LBHDR   
02CC   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
02CE   CD DE 03               CALL   bdosx   
02D1   21 7F 0A               LD   HL,LBHDR+1   
02D4   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   ; the count typed (0-127)
02D5   2C                     INC   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
02D6   85                     ADD   A,L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
02D7   6F                     LD   L,A   
02D8   36 0D                  LD   (HL),13   
02DA                          ENDIF      
02DA                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
                                 ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
                                 ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
                                 ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
                                 ; a full line.
                    LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBC   A,A   
                              AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              CPL      
                              LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
                                 ;   at most
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   
                    LN2:      CALL   getk   
                              JR   Z,ln2   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ln5   
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,ln4   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ln2   ; full
                              LD   (HL),E   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,E   
                    LN3:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
                              JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
                              INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
                              JR   ln2   
                    LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
02DA                          ENDIF      
02DA   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
02DC   F7                     RST   30h   
02DD                             ; =============================================================================
02DD                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
02DD                             ; =============================================================================
02DD                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
02DD                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. The dividend shifts up through A:C
02DD                             ; while the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
02DD                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
02DD   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
02DE   EE 02                  XOR   2   
02E0   B2                     OR   D   
02E1   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
02E3   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
02E5   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
02E7   8F                     ADC   A,A   
02E8   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
02E9   C9                     RET      
02EA   7C           UDV0:     LD   A,H   
02EB   4D                     LD   C,L   
02EC   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
02EF   06 10                  LD   B,16   
02F1   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
02F3   17                     RLA      
02F4   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
02F6   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
02F8   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
02FA   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
02FB   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
02FC   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
02FD   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
02FF   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
0300   67                     LD   H,A   
0301   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
0302   C9                     RET      
0303                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
0303                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
0303   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
0306   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
0307   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0309   FE 0A                  CP   10   
030B   D0                     RET   NC   
030C   03                     INC   BC   
030D   54                     LD   D,H   
030E   5D                     LD   E,L   
030F   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0310   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0311   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0312   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
0313   5F                     LD   E,A   
0314   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0316   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0317   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
0319                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
0319                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
0319                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0319   03           SS0:      INC   BC   
031A   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
031B   03                     INC   BC   
031C   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
031E   28 F9                  JR   Z,ss0   
0320   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0322   20 F6                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
0324   C9                     RET      
0325                          ENDIF      
0325                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
                                 ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   22h   
                              RET   Z   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   BC   
                              JR   skipstr   
0325                          ENDIF      
0325                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
0325                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
0325                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
0325                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
0325                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
0325                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
0325                             ; 
0325                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
0325                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
0325                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
0325                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
0325                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
0325                SKIP:        
0325                          IF   CHECKED   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              POP   IX   
                              DEC   BC   
                              LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
0325                          ENDIF      
0325   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0327   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0328   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
0329                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0329   03                     INC   BC   
032A   B7                     OR   A   
032B   CA 94 04               JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
032E                          ENDIF      
032E                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
                              INC   BC   
032E                          ENDIF      
032E   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0330   CC 1A 03               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
0333   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
0335   28 F0                  JR   Z,sk3   
0337   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
0338   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
033A   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
033C   28 E9                  JR   Z,sk3   
033E   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
0340   20 E6                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0342   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
0343                          IF   1-CHECKED   
0343   C8                     RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
0344   18 E2                  JR   sk1   
0346                          ENDIF      
0346                          IF   CHECKED   
                              JR   NZ,sk1   
                              LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
                              XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
                              AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
                              CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
                              LD   A,D   
                              RET   NZ   
                              JR   sk7   
                    SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
                              JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
                    SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
                              POP   BC   
                              LD   A,"N"   
                              JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
0346                          ENDIF      
0346                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
0346   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
0348   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
034A   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
034C   EF                     RST   28h   
034D   E7                     RST   20h   
034E                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
034E                             ; Uses BC.
034E   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
0351   CD DD 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
0354   7B                     LD   A,E   
0355   F5                     PUSH   AF   
0356   7C                     LD   A,H   
0357   B5                     OR   L   
0358   C4 4E 03               CALL   NZ,pdec   
035B   F1                     POP   AF   
035C   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
035E   EF                     RST   28h   
035F   C9                     RET      
0360                             ; =============================================================================
0360                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
0360                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
0360                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
0360                             ; =============================================================================
0360                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
0360                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
0360                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
0360                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
0360                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
0360                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
0360                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
0360                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
0360                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
0360                          IF   1-TABP0   
0360                PTAB:        
0360                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
0360   88                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
0361   8D                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
0362   9B                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
0363   94                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
0364   83                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
0365   2B                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
0366   98                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
0367   07                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
0368   0F                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
0369   4C                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
036A   22                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
036B   B9                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
036C   1A                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
036D   85                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
036E   60                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
036F   81                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
0370   87                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
0371   33                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
0372   42                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
0373   34                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
0374   A1                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
0375   02                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
0376   E5                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
0377   D8                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
0378   D4                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
0379   70                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
037A   83                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
037B   BE                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
037C   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
037D   78                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
037E   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
037F   80                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
0380                PTABEND:      
0380                          ENDIF      
0380                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
0380                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
0380                             ; return with the carry clear.
0380   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
0381   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
0383   FE 0A                  CP   10   
0385   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
0387   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
0389   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
038B   FE 06                  CP   6   
038D   D0                     RET   NC   
038E   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
0390   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
0391   C9                     RET      
0392                             ; =============================================================================
0392                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
0392                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
0392                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
0392                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
0392                             ; 
0392                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
0392                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
0392                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
0392                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
0392                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
0392                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
0392                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
0392                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
0392                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
0392                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
0392                             ;  data stack.
0392                             ; =============================================================================
0392                          IFN   CPM   
                    RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
0392                          ENDIF      
0392                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
0392   CD D0 03     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
0395   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
0396   32 7A 0A               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
0399   FE 03        PK1:      CP   3   ; (getk joins here)
039B   C0                     RET   NZ   
039C                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
039C                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
039C                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
039C                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
039C   3A 7B 0A     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
039F   B7                     OR   A   
03A0   CA 90 04     CT0:      JP   Z,brk   
03A3   D5                     PUSH   DE   
03A4   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
03A7   CD D0 03     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
03AA   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
03AC   1B                     DEC   DE   
03AD   7A                     LD   A,D   
03AE   B3                     OR   E   
03AF   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
03B1   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
03B2   FE 03                  CP   3   
03B4   28 EA                  JR   Z,ct0   ; (the zero flag takes the JP there)
03B6   B7                     OR   A   
03B7   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
03B9   32 7A 0A               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
03BC   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
03BE   B7                     OR   A   
03BF   C9                     RET      
03C0                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
03C0   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
03C1   21 7A 0A               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
03C4   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
03C5   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
03C7   E1                     POP   HL   
03C8   B7                     OR   A   
03C9   C0                     RET   NZ   
03CA   CD D0 03               CALL   rawk   
03CD   C8                     RET   Z   
03CE   18 C9                  JR   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
03D0                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
03D0                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
03D0                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
03D0                BRK:      EQU   edit0   
03D0                          ENDIF      
03D0                          IF   CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
03D0                          ENDIF      
03D0                          IF   CPM   
03D0   3E FF        RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
03D2                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
03D2                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
03D2   D5           PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
03D3   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03D4   5F                     LD   E,A   
03D5   3E 06                  LD   A,6   
03D7   CD DE 03               CALL   bdosx   
03DA   E1                     POP   HL   
03DB   D1                     POP   DE   
03DC   B7                     OR   A   ; (for getk)
03DD   C9                     RET      
03DE                             ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
03DE   C5           BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
03DF   D9                     EXX      
03E0   E5                     PUSH   HL   
03E1   D9                     EXX      
03E2   4F                     LD   C,A   
03E3   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
03E6   D9                     EXX      
03E7   E1                     POP   HL   
03E8   D9                     EXX      
03E9   C1                     POP   BC   
03EA   C9                     RET      
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                             ; =============================================================================
03EB                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
03EB                             ; =============================================================================
03EB                          IF   CHECKED   
                                 ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
                                 ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
                                 ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
                                 ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
                                 ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
                                 ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
                                 ; Keeps HL and BC.
                    CHKST:    INC   HL   
                              LD   A,H   
                              DEC   HL   
                              CP   LETPAGE   
                              JR   C,chs1   
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              RET   C   
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              LD   E,A   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   E   
                              RET   NC   
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                          IF   CHECKED   
                    CHS1:     JP   e_store   
                                 ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
                                 ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
                                 ; program's end.
                    CHKHP:       
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                                 ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
                                 ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
                                 ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
                              RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
                              ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
                              LD   A,(0007h)   
                              DEC   A   
                              CP   H   
                              JR   C,e_heap   
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                                 ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
                                 ; round always falls outside it.)
                              LD   A,H   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              JR   NC,e_heap   
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                          IF   CHECKED   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,(NPEND)   
                              ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              POP   DE   
                              RET   C   
                    E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              JP   e_heap1   
                                 ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
                                 ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
                                 ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
                                 ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
                                 ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
                                 ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
                    CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
                              ADD   HL,SP   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              JR   C,e_under   
                              INC   D   
                              JR   NZ,e_over   
                              EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
                              LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
                              CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
                              LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
                              EXX      
                              JR   NZ,e_rover   
                              CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
                              RET   C   
                              EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   
                              EXX      
                              LD   A,"r"   
                              JR   errp   
                    E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
                              DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
                    E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
                              JR   errp   
                    E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
                              LD   A,"s"   
                              JR   error   
                                 ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
                                 ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
                                 ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
                                 ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
                    E_HI:     INC   B   
                              DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
                              RST   08h   
                              LD   B,D   
                              LD   C,E   
                              LD   A,"U"   
                              JR   error   
                                 ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
                                 ; a 3-byte LD DE,nn (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
                    E_BREAK:   LD   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
                              DB   11h   
                    E_HEAP1:   LD   A,"H"   ; heap (found inside chkhp)
                              DB   11h   
                    E_STORE:   LD   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space (chkst)
                                 ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
                    ERRP:     POP   DE   
                              JR   error   
                    E_QUOTE:   LD   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
                              LD   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
                              LD   A,"Q"   
                              DB   11h   
                    E_RESV:   LD   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
                              DB   11h   
                    E_ZERO:   LD   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
                              DB   11h   
                    E_BRACK:   LD   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
                                 ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
                                 ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
                                 ; 
                                 ;   Err X @ line,col
                                 ;   up to 16 characters of the text from the place
                                 ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
                                 ;   Rtn n
                    ERROR:    PUSH   HL   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
                              LD   E,A   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   "Err ",22h   
                              LD   A,E   
                              RST   28h   
                              CALL   pmsg   
                              DB   " @ ",22h   
                              DEC   BC   ; BC = the place
                                 ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
                                 ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
                                 ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   
                              LD   DE,0   
                              LD   A,B   
                              CP   PROG/256   
                              JR   C,er3   
                              INC   H   
                              LD   L,E   ; HL = PROG
                    ER1:      INC   DE   ; a new line starts at HL
                              PUSH   HL   
                    ER2:      LD   A,L   
                              SUB   C   
                              LD   A,H   
                              SBC   A,B   
                              JR   NC,er2x   ; reached the place
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,er2   
                              POP   AF   
                              JR   er1   
                    ER2X:     POP   HL   
                    ER3:      PUSH   BC   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the line
                              LD   A,","   
                              RST   28h   
                              POP   DE   
                              POP   HL   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              OR   A   
                              SBC   HL,DE   
                              INC   HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the column
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              POP   HL   ; the text, as it is: 16 characters, or fewer
                              LD   B,16   ;   if the line or the program ends first
                    ER4:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,er5   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,er5   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,er5   
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              CP   1Ah   ; (the ^Z that pads a file's last record ends
                              JR   Z,er5   ;   the text too: some terminals clear the
03EB                          ENDIF      ;   screen on it)
03EB                          IF   CHECKED   
                              RST   28h   
                              DJNZ   er4   
                    ER5:         ; (without the editor: on into pstk)
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                          IF   CHECKED*EDITOR   
                              CALL   pstk   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              JP   edit0   ; back to the editor, with both stacks cleared
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                             ; =============================================================================
03EB                             ;  Routines that the checked build's report and the editor share
03EB                             ; =============================================================================
03EB                SPADJ:    EQU   2*EDITOR   ; (with the editor pstk is called, not fallen
03EB                             ;   into: the stack is one address deeper)
03EB                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
03EB                             ; pstk: the two stack lines:  Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
03EB                             ;                             Rtn n
03EB                             ; TOS must be in memory with the rest (pushed). In a build without the
03EB                             ; editor this is the end of `error`, which runs on into it.
03EB   CD 4E 04     PSTK:     CALL   pnl   
03EE   53 74 6B 20 22         DB   "Stk ",22h   
03F3   21 F8 09               LD   HL,DSTOP-2-SPADJ   ; (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed with the
03F6   B7                     OR   A   ;   first value and holds nothing)
03F7   ED 72                  SBC   HL,SP   
03F9   CD 34 04               CALL   phalf   ; the depth
03FC   3E 3A                  LD   A,":"   
03FE   EF                     RST   28h   
03FF   79                     LD   A,C   
0400   FE 09                  CP   9   
0402   38 0A                  JR   C,er6   
0404   CD 54 04               CALL   pmsg   
0407   20 2E 2E 2E 22         DB   " ...",22h   
040C   0E 08                  LD   C,8   
040E   26 00        ER6:      LD   H,0   ; C = the number of cells to show
0410   69                     LD   L,C   
0411   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
0412   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
0413                          ENDIF      
0413                          IF   EDITOR   
0413   23                     INC   HL   
0414   23                     INC   HL   
0415                          ENDIF      
0415                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0415   0C                     INC   C   
0416   0D           ER7:      DEC   C   
0417   28 11                  JR   Z,er8   
0419   2B                     DEC   HL   
041A   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
041B   2B                     DEC   HL   
041C   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
041D   E5                     PUSH   HL   
041E   C5                     PUSH   BC   
041F   3E 20                  LD   A," "   
0421   EF                     RST   28h   
0422   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0423   CD 46 03               CALL   psgn   
0426   C1                     POP   BC   
0427   E1                     POP   HL   
0428   18 EC                  JR   er7   
042A   CD 4E 04     ER8:      CALL   pnl   
042D                          ENDIF      
042D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
042D   52 74 6E 20 30 22      DB   "Rtn 0",22h   ; (only ^V comes here, and at the editor the
0433   C9                     RET      ;   return stack is always empty)
0434                          ENDIF      
0434                          IF   CHECKED   
                              DB   "Rtn ",22h   
                              EXX      
                              PUSH   HL   
                              EXX      
                              POP   DE   
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   
                              OR   A   
                              SBC   HL,DE   
0434                          ENDIF      
0434                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
                              CALL   phalf   
                              CALL   pnl   
                              DB   22h   
                              JP   endprog   
0434                          ENDIF      
0434                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0434                             ; phalf: print half of HL, and leave it in C. (With the editor, pstk ends by
0434                             ; running on into this.)
0434   CB 3C        PHALF:    SRL   H   
0436   CB 1D                  RR   L   
0438   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0439   CD 4E 03               CALL   pdec   
043C   C1                     POP   BC   
043D   C9                     RET      
043E                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
043E                             ; "$", and the texts of the report and the editor). In the checked build a
043E                             ; NUL first is an error: Q.
043E   7E           PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
043F   23                     INC   HL   
0440   FE 22                  CP   22h   
0442   C8                     RET   Z   
0443                          ENDIF      
0443                          IF   CHECKED   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,e_dollar   
0443                          ENDIF      
0443                          IF   CHECKED+EDITOR   
0443   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
0445   20 04                  JR   NZ,prs1   
0447   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0448   23                     INC   HL   
0449   E6 BF                  AND   0BFh   
044B   EF           PRS1:     RST   28h   
044C   18 F0                  JR   prstr   
044E                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
044E                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
044E   3E 0D        PNL:      LD   A,13   
0450   EF                     RST   28h   
0451   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
0453   EF                     RST   28h   
0454   E3           PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
0455   CD 3E 04               CALL   prstr   
0458   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   
0459   C9                     RET      
045A                          ENDIF      
045A                          IF   CHECKED   
                    E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
                              POP   HL   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
                              LD   A,"Q"   
                              JP   error   
045A                          ENDIF      
045A                             ; =============================================================================
045A                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
045A                             ; 
045A                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
045A                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
045A                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
045A                             ; 
045A                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
045A                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
045A                             ;    n         take line n out
045A                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
045A                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
045A                             ; 
045A                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
045A                             ; 
045A                             ;    ^G        run the program
045A                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
045A                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
045A                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
045A                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
045A                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
045A                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
045A                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
045A                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
045A                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
045A                             ;    ^V        view: the build, both stacks, and the program's size, lines
045A                             ;              and free memory
045A                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
045A                             ; 
045A                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
045A                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
045A                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
045A                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
045A                             ; 
045A                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
045A                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
045A                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
045A                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
045A                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
045A                             ; 
045A                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
045A                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
045A                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
045A                             ; 
045A                             ;  Things to know:
045A                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
045A                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
045A                             ;      after editing it.
045A                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
045A                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
045A                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
045A                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
045A                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
045A                             ;      read of the other builds (BDOS 10 under CP/M).
045A                             ; 
045A                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
045A                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
045A                             ; =============================================================================
045A                          IF   EDGEN   
                    INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
045A                          ENDIF      
045A                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
                                 ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
                                 ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
                                 ; (see e_hi).
                              LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
045A                          ENDIF      
045A                          IF   EDGEN   
                              JR   edit0   
045A                          ENDIF      
045A                          IF   EDITOR   
045A                             ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
045A   7D           RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
045B   BB                     CP   E   
045C   28 4A                  JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
045E   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
045F   2C                     INC   L   
0460   18 2B                  JR   lf1   
0462                             ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
0462                             ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
0462                             ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
0462   01 C8 00     ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
0465   CD D0 03     ES1:      CALL   rawk   
0468   20 0A                  JR   NZ,es2   
046A   0B                     DEC   BC   
046B   78                     LD   A,B   
046C   B1                     OR   C   
046D   20 F6                  JR   NZ,es1   
046F   CD DD 04               CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
0472   18 22                  JR   edit   
0474   FE 5B        ES2:      CP   "["   
0476   20 30                  JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
0478   CD 36 05     ES3:      CALL   ekey   
047B   FE 40                  CP   40h   
047D   38 F9                  JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
047F   D6 43                  SUB   "C"   
0481   28 D7                  JR   Z,right   
0483   3D                     DEC   A   ; "D"?
0484   20 22                  JR   NZ,ed1   ; no: on into left
0486                             ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
0486   7D           LEFT:     LD   A,L   
0487   87                     ADD   A,A   
0488   28 1E                  JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
048A   2D                     DEC   L   
048B   3E 08                  LD   A,8   
048D   EF           LF1:      RST   28h   
048E   18 18                  JR   ed1   
0490                             ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared.
0490                             ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
0490                             ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
0490   31 FA 09     EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
0493   21                     DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
0494   D1           SKEND:    POP   DE   
0495   E5           EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
0496                             ; edit: start a new input line.
0496   D9           EDIT:     EXX      
0497   21 E0 08               LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
049A   D9                     EXX      
049B   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
049E   22 7A 0A               LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
04A1   22 3A 0A               LD   (EDLN),HL   ; no line is being edited
04A4   21 80 0A               LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; HL = the cursor,
04A7   5D                     LD   E,L   ;   E = the end of the line (its low byte)
04A8   CD 36 05     ED1:      CALL   ekey   
04AB   FE 7F                  CP   7Fh   
04AD   28 40                  JR   Z,bsp   ; DEL
04AF   FE 20                  CP   " "   
04B1   30 56                  JR   NC,insc   
04B3   FE 09                  CP   9   
04B5   28 52                  JR   Z,insc   ; Tab is text
04B7   FE 08                  CP   8   
04B9   28 34                  JR   Z,bsp   
04BB   FE 02                  CP   2   
04BD   28 C7                  JR   Z,left   ; ^B
04BF   FE 06                  CP   6   
04C1   28 97                  JR   Z,right   ; ^F
04C3   FE 1B                  CP   1Bh   
04C5   28 9B                  JR   Z,esc   
04C7   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; a command key? Look it up
04C8   21 3C 05               LD   HL,cmds   
04CB   06 09                  LD   B,NCMD   
04CD   BE           ED2:      CP   (HL)   
04CE   23                     INC   HL   
04CF   28 07                  JR   Z,ed3   
04D1   23                     INC   HL   
04D2   23                     INC   HL   
04D3   10 F8                  DJNZ   ed2   
04D5   E1                     POP   HL   
04D6   18 D0                  JR   ed1   ; no: the key is ignored
04D8   7E           ED3:      LD   A,(HL)   
04D9   23                     INC   HL   
04DA   66                     LD   H,(HL)   
04DB   6F                     LD   L,A   
